From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: SHChangeNotify delivers SHCNF_DWORD items

SHChangeNotify dropped an event whose items are SHCNF_DWORD values, with a FIXME. calibre (and Python installers) announce SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED that way, so neither the shell nor the file type refresh heard about the new associations. The values now arrive as an SHChangeDWORDAsIDList, as documented, and the event is delivered.
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/changenotify.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/changenotify.c
@@ -324,7 +324,22 @@
     case SHCNF_PRINTERW:
         FIXME("SHChangeNotify with (uFlags & SHCNF_PRINTER)\n");
         return;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_NO_DWORD_ITEMS
     case SHCNF_DWORD:
+        /* (wine-sg 8289) the items are two values, delivered as an SHChangeDWORDAsIDList: calibre and
+         * Python installers announce SHCNE_ASSOCCHANGED this way, and it was dropped */
+        if ((Pidls[0] = SHAlloc( 12 )))
+        {
+            BYTE *p = (BYTE *)Pidls[0];
+            DWORD item1 = PtrToUlong( dwItem1 ), item2 = PtrToUlong( dwItem2 );
+
+            *(USHORT *)p = 10;            /* cb */
+            memcpy( p + 2, &item1, 4 );
+            memcpy( p + 6, &item2, 4 );
+            *(USHORT *)(p + 10) = 0;      /* cbZero */
+        }
+        break;
+#endif
     default:
         FIXME("unknown type %08x\n", uFlags & SHCNF_TYPE);
         return;
